Changes to the upstream sources (long_bone/src), all marked [CCX] in the code:
- The upstream sources were moved into long_bone/src and converted to LF line
  endings.
- FE coupling ported from Abaqus to CalculiX 2.17: the input deck is written
  in Update_model.cpp, stresses and strains are read from the CalculiX .dat
  output in Read_stimulus.cpp, and the minimum principal strain is computed
  from the strain tensor. The reference node uses *RIGID BODY.
- Elements with identical (E, nu) are grouped into one material. This is
  equivalent to the original per-element materials.
- The initial FE solution is computed inside the program.
- Random numbers come from a seeded std::mt19937 (nrand.cpp, main.cpp).
- More robust node and element file readers, and clamping to the lattice
  bounds (Read_node_file.cpp, Read_element_file.cpp, Extremes_element.cpp).
- Write_statistics.cpp (new) writes a daily summary of cell and tissue counts.
- run.bat (Abaqus) was removed and replaced by long_bone/araclar/run.sh.

The cell rules (differentiation, proliferation, mitosis, migration, apoptosis,
ageing) are unchanged.

